meta-secureedge-platform
=======================

Platform integration for Yocto Project Scarthgap, targeting Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W
(64-bit), with a QEMU ARM64 development configuration.

Contents and selection
----------------------

- C agent publishing synthetic temperature and voltage telemetry via libmosquitto.
- Raspberry Pi networking, DEV/PROD images and PROD service isolation.
- DATA storage, signed RAUC bundles, A/B WIC layout and boot/update tooling.

The base image enables the agent service. PROD selects hardening and restricted
maintenance access. Only the orchestrated profile selects persistent agent
identity/configuration. Its installation service is disabled by default.
Watchdog configuration is explicitly selected by the watchdog test profile;
the standalone orchestrated profile does not select it. The service-monitor
recipe is available but not selected by the inspected images/profiles, and its
service is disabled by default. Presence in the layer is not runtime enablement.

Build dependencies
------------------

The layer declares core, but its current metadata also requires meta-rauc during
parsing: the bundle recipe inherits bundle, and RAUC appends need matching recipes.
Base Pi/QEMU profiles omit meta-rauc and therefore have a static parsing blocker.
See docs/build.md at the repository root before attempting a build.

Profiles also select Poky and meta-openembedded; Raspberry Pi uses
meta-raspberrypi. Use with meta-secureedge-distro. Kas layer paths assume
/workspace; profiles default to DEV, so select the PROD target explicitly.

The agent recipe compiles recipes-apps/secureedge-agent/files, not application/.
These copies differ in MQTT implementation and configuration.

Update status
-------------

Bundle verification, B installation, image checks and trial arming are reported
hardware observations. First B boot and complete automatic rollback qualification
remain pending. See docs/validation.md for archived evidence limits and
docs/security.md for deliberately blocked and operator-assisted confirmation.

License and provenance
----------------------

COPYING.MIT is retained. Recipe declarations include MIT and CLOSED; ownership,
copyright attribution, license scope and third-party firmware obligations need
an explicit publication decision. The layer notice does not settle rights for
all payloads.
